      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>First beats on the new Mac. Headphones only (thin walls at the house).</div><div><br/></div><div><en-media hash="2b8bf992194c53e024ec4237ac009208" type="image/png"/></div><div>Pattern for "sf-bounce" (kick / snare / hat / perc, 16 steps). 96 bpm, the hats with 2 ghost 16ths.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>Key: D minor. chords Dm9 - Bbmaj7 - Gm7 - A7(b9).</li><li>Fog-horn sample from Crissy Field (recorded on the phone 8/30). pitch it to D, low pass, use as the intro.</li><li>Bass: Sytrus sub + a little FM grit on the top octave.</li><li>Sam suggests a live guitar line. maybe.</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>9/13: arrangement done to 2:50. needs a better hook. leaving it for after the UIST talk.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
